      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 3-A #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Shear Line\nIssued at: 12:00 AM, 25 November 2025(Tuesday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Quezon, Rizal, Laguna, Metro Manila, Bulacan(Norzagaray, Dona Remedios Trinidad, San Jose del Monte), Batangas(Talisay, Tanauan, Santo Tomas, Malvar, Balete, Mataasnakahoy, Lipa, Padre Garcia, Rosario, San Juan, Taysan, Lobo, Batangas City, Ibaan, San Jose, Cuenca, San Pascual, Alitagtag, Bauan, Mabini, San Luis, Tingloy, Santa Teresita, Taal, San Nicolas, Agoncillo, Lemery, Laurel) and Cavite(Tagaytay, Silang, Carmona, Amadeo, Gen. Mariano Alvarez).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: Possible FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate with occasional heavy rains over Nueva Ecija, Tarlac, Pampanga, Zambales and Bataan within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Bulacan(Angat, Balagtas, Baliuag, Bocaue, Bulakan, Bustos, Calumpit, Malolos, Meycauayan, Guiguinto, Hagonoy, Marilao, Obando, Pandi, Paombong, Plaridel, Pulilan, San Ildefonso, San Miguel, San Rafael, Santa Maria), Cavite(Alfonso, General Trias, General Emilio Aguinaldo, Indang, Magallanes, Maragondon, Mendez, Ternate, Trece Martires, Bacoor, Cavite City, Dasmarinas, Imus, Kawit, Naic, Noveleta, Rosario, Tanza) and Batangas(Balayan, Calaca, Calatagan, Lian, Nasugbu, Tuy) which may persist within 3 hours.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 2:00 AM tomorrow.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
